ecord-257rig-i3"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257rig-i3"],"id":"long.record-257rig-i3","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.109 (Unboundedness of a positive shifted recurrence)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.109, p. 75, label record:257rig-i3","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $A\\subseteq\\mathbb{N}_{>0}$ be infinite, fix a shift $c\\ge0$ and a positive integer $v$, and let $u$ be a positive integer sequence satisfying\n$$\nu(n+1)+v c_A(c+n+1)=2u(n)\\qquad(n\\ge0).\n$$\nThen $u$ is unbounded. Indeed, under a proposed bound $u(n)\\le B$, choose $2B+1$ distinct support elements and a common multiple larger than $c$. At the corresponding index the divisor count is at least $2B+1$, contradicting the recurrence. This does not conflict with Theorem 6.105, whose condition is $u(n)/2^n\\to0$, not boundedness. An unbounded sequence can still satisfy that limit.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257rig-i3","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257rig-i3","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-i3%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.exists_unbounded_shifted_odd_tail_nat_state_of_support_fraction%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-i3%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.exists_unbounded_shifted_odd_tail_nat_state_of_support_fraction%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.exists_unbounded_shifted_odd_tail_nat_state_of_support_fraction"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe